 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2346) 'The steps, in order
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2346) '1. The pending prompt change was committed in decider-pong.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2346) '2. The submodule checkout was shallow, so the mirror refused it. It was unshallowed from GitHub, and the pinned upstream commit was pushed to a new bare mirror of the upstream. All 98 commits arrived and `git fsck` is clean.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2346) '3. `bin/bao-github-credential` was removed in one commit, then the submodule was replaced by the manifest row in the next.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2346) '4. A bare mirror of decider-pong was made and `main` was pushed to it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2346) '5. Two rows were added to `default.xml` beside the other interactors, committed and pushed to the manifest mirror.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2346) '6. A scoped `repo sync` of the two paths placed both checkouts. A full sync was not run, because three projects sit on `dev1` branches that the preflight would park.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2346) 'Gates run
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2346) '`check_manifest_comments.py`, `check_manifest_xml.py --offline`, `check_manifest_dupes.exs` and `check_manifest_root.py` passed, each after its self-test. `check_offline.exs` lists 19 projects with 0 failures, both decider rows at their pins, and its self-test fails as planted. One run reported 1 failure while a push to the mirror was in flight; three runs after it reported 0.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2346) 'GitHub and the mirror
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2346) 'decider-pong's GitHub `main` fast-forwards to the mirror's and is pushed there too. The manifest was pushed to the mirror only. GitHub's manifest carries one commit the mirror lacks, which adds a row for a repo not yet mirrored. Reconciling the two needs that repo mirrored first, and is the user's call.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2346) 'Open questions, parked in dev.next
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2346) 'The languages rule forbids project Python. decider-pong is an evaluation harness. It is either ported to Elixir or the engine, or given a named exemption. The org names repos by hexagon side; the repo should carry the interactor prefix. Only the user renames repos on GitHub. After the rename the manifest row changes by one line. The removed helper stays in history from the commit that added it; dropping it means rewriting a published branch.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2346) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2346) 'The contract places a repo in the manifest the day it is created and pins upstreams as manifest rows. The repo also carried a blocklisted OpenBao helper. Two questions remain open: the repo is all Python, and its name lacks a side prefix.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2346  1 LINE
 Text:Written
